      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely valid to feel resistant to therapy if it feels like just another pressure to perform or \"fix\" yourself. The weight you are describing sounds like deep existential exhaustion, which is profoundly difficult. Instead of focusing on \"fixing,\" perhaps consider looking into expressive outlets like journaling, art, or intense physical movement to process this pressure. Remember that you don't have to find \"peace\" right away; sometimes the goal is just to lower the immediate weight.",
      "source": "target",
